/div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Each visitor also shows their name when known (signed in, or arrived from one of our emails), otherwise &quot;Visitor from Toronto, phone&quot;; the page and car they are on, and how many others look at that car now; the device, city, the site or campaign that sent them and &quot;from an ad&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Suggested: the best next step and the message to send. Press <b class="gd-ui">Invite to chat with this message</b> to send it at once, <b class="gd-ui">Edit the message</b> to change it first, <b class="gd-ui">Offer a 10% discount code</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Assign to Sales</b> or, when their dates are taken, <b class="gd-ui">Suggest a similar free car</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Pages</b> for every page and event of the visit with each signal&#39;s points, or <b class="gd-ui">Start a chat</b> to write your own message. They see it in a bubble and reply from it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Below: hot visitors today (and whether someone acted), the signals of the last 24 hours, and the most viewed cars of the week with prices shown and the car most compared with each. The page refreshes by itself every 15 seconds.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-name-a-visitor" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Name a visitor</h2><p class="gd-p">When you learn who a visitor is (they called, or told you in the chat), give them a name. Only staff see it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On their line, press <b class="gd-ui">Name</b>. Type the name and, if you have them, their phone, email and a note. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the name</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The name shows on Live visitors, the visit&#39;s pages, Visitor history and Live chat, and on every later visit from the same browser. The line says who named them, with the phone, email and note.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A phone you add also saves them as a contact in Quo, and a call or text from that number shows the name in Texts and calls.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Kept consistent: if they later book or sign in, the name the booking has replaces yours (&quot;Booked&quot;). A chat from another browser with the same email or phone gets the same name, and a chat&#39;s email or phone fills in the ones you left empty.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Edit name</b> changes it; <b class="gd-ui">Remove the name</b> takes it off.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-live-map" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Live map</h2><p class="gd-p">A map of the Greater Toronto Area and around it (Kitchener and Guelph to Cobourg and Peterborough, Niagara to Barrie) with a pin for every lead, made for a TV or monitor in the office.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Live map</b>. The tiles count who is on the site now, requests today, bookings confirmed this week, cars on rent now and the money collected this month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each pin is one person, as their most advanced step: on rent now, booking (upcoming), request, form sent, unfinished form, game player, previous renter or on the site now. The legend counts each kind; press one to hide or show it. A pin pulses while the person is on the site and for 5 minutes after something new.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Hover over or press a pin for its card: the name, the score from 0 to 100 with its strongest signals, the car they looked at last with its photo and daily price, and how long ago. The cards below the map list everyone of the last 30 days and everything current; sort them by score, or press <b class="gd-ui">Show on the map</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Names show as the first name and last initial, phones as their last 4 digits, and no email. Tick <b class="gd-ui">Show details</b> to see them in full (never in TV mode).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Open TV mode</b> on the computer connected to the TV and make the browser full screen (F11 on Windows, Control Command F on a Mac). TV mode fills the screen without the menu, hides the pointer when the mouse is still, refreshes every 30 seconds and shows the hottest leads one after another with the car&#39;s photo.</div></li></ol></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Where a pin goes: the approximate place of the visitor&#39;s network (about 1 km, from Cloudflare), else the centre of the renter&#39;s home city or of the visit&#39;s city. Nothing is looked up and no address is shown. People with no place are counted under the legend.</li><li>The score adds up the points of the signals: what they did (on rent, booking, request, form sent or started), a game played or its prize claimed, past rentals, a returning visit, pages, minutes on the site, cars viewed, on the site now, from an ad, and the strongest Live visitors reasons. 60 or more is hot, 30 or more warm.</li><li>The fleet layer: once CarmaCars&#39; trackers report, each car shows on the map with its photo, the direction it is going and its status (on rent, available, in service). Tick <b class="gd-ui">Fleet</b> to show or hide it.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-the-signals" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The signals</h2><p class="gd-p">Each signal adds points to the booking likelihood. They come from what the visitor does on the site, never from what they type.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Intent: dates searched again and again, saw the full price, reached the booking form (and which step), came back for the same car on another day, comparing two or three cars, read the cancellation policy, read about the deposit, insurance or requirements, tapped to call, text or WhatsApp us or copied our number, checked delivery, looked through many photos or stayed long on one car.</li><li>Urgency: pickup within 72 hours, weekend or holiday dates, on a phone late at night, came from a city or model page or a &quot;near me&quot; search.</li><li>Value: a weekly or monthly rental, a premium car, SUV or van, adding a driver, asked about young drivers, a business email.</li><li>Hesitation: watching the price (sorted by lowest price, lowered the price limit), left after seeing the price, unsure about the deposit, trouble with a form, the car not free for their dates.</li><li>Context: came from an ad, a past renter, an offer or payment waiting, a game code not used yet, a popular car. The signals of known customers (offer opened, pay page left, change proposal, request stopped, returning visitor, viewing spree) count too.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-hot-visitors-and-the-actions" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Hot visitors and the actions</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>When a visitor turns hot, everyone with Live visitors open sees an alert at the top of the page. Turn on desktop alerts in Live chat to get one on your computer too; none come in the quiet hours (11 pm to 7 am). No email is sent.</li><li>A discount code is single use, 10% off the rental charge (at most $75), valid 3 days, one per visitor a week and 10 a day per person. Admins and Sales send them; the code goes in the chat with the message.</li><li>Assign to Sales gives the visitor to the Sales person on shift (or to you if you work Sales) and raises a task with the reasons and the contact when we know who they are.</li><li>Each action shows on the visitor (&quot;Invited by Lena, 2 min ago&quot;) so two people do not write to the same visitor.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-signal-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Signal settings</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Live visitors</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Signal settings</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Score and actions: from how many points a visitor is hot or warm, when a signal is strong or medium, the hot alert, and the discount code (percent, most off a booking, days valid, codes a day per person, whether customer service may send codes, and the message).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each signal: on or off, its points, its thresholds (for example 72 hours for &quot;Pickup soon&quot;, 3 searches for &quot;Searching dates again and again&quot;), the suggested action and the message. {car}, {days}, {pickup} and the other words in braces are filled in from the visit.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the signals</b>. The next look at each visit uses them.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-follow-up-tasks" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Follow-up tasks</h2><p class="gd-p">Signals of known visitors become tasks with a suggested action, for example &quot;Call or message Maya Chen: opened offer CC-1042 twice, no answer for 6 hours&quot;.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>An offer opened and not answered: after 6 hours, to Sales when the booking is credited to someone in Sales, otherwise customer service.</li><li>The pay page left without paying: after 30 minutes, customer service. The change proposal opened twice: customer service.</li><li>A booking request started and stopped, or a viewing spree, by a known visitor: Sales.</li><li>A task closes by itself when the renter answers the offer, pays or answers the proposal. Each signal raises one task only.</li><li>The thresholds are in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, group &quot;Live visitors and live chat&quot;, with how long &quot;on the site now&quot; lasts (5 minutes) and how often an open page says it is still there (45 seconds). Follow-ups done count in My sales.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-recovery-emails" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Recovery emails</h2><p class="gd-p">Known renters who stop before finishing get one polite reminder, and at most one more a day later.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>An offer opened and not answered: after 4 hours. The pay page left without paying: after an hour. A change proposal opened and not answered: after 4 hours.</li><li>A booking request started and not sent: after 2 hours, and only to renters who agreed to hear from us (marketing consent).</li><li>Sent only between 9:00 and 21:00 Toronto time, never to someone who unsubscribed, and never while a staff member is handling the renter (a task they took, a chat with a person, a message from staff).</li><li>They stop as soon as the renter answers, pays or sends the request; a reminder still waiting is not sent. The delays and hours are in Program settings, &quot;Booking recovery emails&quot;.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-interest-in-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interest in a car</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, a car, Overview: &quot;Interest on the site&quot; shows who is looking now, views today and in 7 days, the people who saw the price for their dates, conversion over 30 days (requests from the people who viewed it), the cars most often compared with it, and the last 14 days. The Vehicles list has &quot;Most viewed cars this week&quot;.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-a-renter-s-visits" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A renter&#39;s visits</h2><p class="gd-p">On a renter&#39;s page (People &gt; Renters, the name) and on a booking&#39;s History tab, &quot;On the site&quot; lists when they viewed the offer, opened the change proposal, viewed or left the pay page, which cars they looked at, and their chats.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-live-chat" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Live chat</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A visitor who asks for a person is a line on To do, marked Now: press <b class="gd-ui">Open the chat</b>. Or open <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Live chat</b>. The menu counts chats waiting for a person. Open chats come first, those waiting for a person on top, with their minutes against the first reply target (5 minutes).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose a conversation. Beside it you see the visitor&#39;s page, pages, signals, and the renter with their bookings when known.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take over</b>: the assistant stops and the visitor reads that you joined. Writing a reply also takes over. Press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b> (or Enter).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hand back to the assistant</b> lets it answer again. <b class="gd-ui">Close</b> ends the chat; if the visitor gave an email they get a copy. <b class="gd-ui">Email the transcript</b> sends it any time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Notify me: &quot;Email me when a chat waits (while I am on shift)&quot; and desktop alerts in this browser. You are on shift while Live chat or Live visitors is open.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The assistant only repeats prices from our pricing (a quote or the car&#39;s rates), never offers discounts or promises a car, never talks about insurance and never names a provider. Each reply it was not allowed to send says so in the conversation. When nobody is on shift, the chat asks for the visitor&#39;s name, email or phone and raises a task. A booking from a chat you handled is credited only when you choose &quot;I sourced this client&quot; on the quote or offer.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-the-assistant-s-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The assistant&#39;s settings</h2><p class="gd-p">In Program settings, &quot;Live visitors and live chat&quot;: the chat on or off, the AI first or not, its model, the neurons it may use a day (6,000, about 10 chats; then chats wait for a person), the greeting on car pages after some seconds (off by default), how long chats and visits are kept, as the privacy policy says: chats 12 months, the pages of a visit 90 days, the visit&#39;s summary in Visitor history 13 months, and the daily totals, which name no one, 3 years.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-what-a-visitor-typed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What a visitor typed</h2><p class="gd-p">A visitor who typed contact details into a form shows them on their line: &quot;Typed into the booking request, not sent: Maya Chen, maya@example.com&quot;, with <b class="gd-ui">Email not confirmed</b> until they open the link we emailed, and <b class="gd-ui">Renter page</b>.</p></section>');
-- GUIDES 0243 END
